{
  "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
  "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Paul J. Beard, Esq. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The county refused to give George Sheetz a permit to build a home unless he paid a substantial fee to finance public road improvements. He was faced with an impossible choice: the taking of over $23,000 or the ability to use his land. Though the fee went beyond mitigation, he did submit to the fee and paid under protest. After all, the permit was worth far more than the fee."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 22-1074, Sheetz versus the County of El Dorado."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Do we have to decide any more than whether Nollan/Dolan scrutiny applies to -- can apply here to legislative exaction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Can I try it this way? My question is whether your argument is that all permit extractions should be -- are implicating the Takings Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what if it's not a permit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "why would it be the exact same kind of unconstitutional conditions requirement, test, evaluation, what have you, when we're not talking about an individual permitting decision, but we're talking about a generally applicable scheme?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what would you evaluate? I mean, to me, that just makes it sound as though a county can't -- can't pass generally applicable laws anymore because, I mean, a -- a Nollan/Dolan analysis, I would --I would think, you would have to look at the size of the individual property, you know, in a case like this, the distance from the highway, the number of residents, the -- the exact amount of use that they're going to do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "would you at least agree that that's an available argument on remand?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So is -- is it okay to classify all single-family homes together?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it proportionality? Is that your answer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT DO YOU THINK IT MIGHT BE A TAKING OR IMPLICATE THE TAKINGS CLAUSE?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Beard",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "PROPERTY TAXES, ONE CASE THAT WAS CITED IN KOONTZ FROM 1960, BRUSHABER, SAID YEAH, THE PROGRESSIVE TAX IS CONSTITUTIONAL. THERE'S NO TAKING. WE COULD IMAGINE A SITUATION WHERE IT BECOMES SO CONFISCATORY THAT THAT PORTION OF IT MAY BECOME A TAKING."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. McGRATH",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "LIKE COUNTLESS LOCAL GOVERNMENTS ACROSS THE COUNTRY, THE COUNTY OF EL DORADO CHARGES A FEE TO DEVELOPERS TO ADDRESS THE IMPACTS OF NEW DEVELOPMENT USING A PREDETERMINED SCHEDULE, AS JUSTICE KAGAN HAS -- HAS EMPHASIZED, RETICULATED BY GEOGRAPHIC ZONE AND DEVELOPMENT TYPE."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DO YOU THINK THAT LEGISLATIVE EXACTIONS CAN BE SUBJECT TO NOLLAN/DOLAN SCRUTINY?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. McGRATH",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I THINK THAT THERE ARE LEGISLATIVE EXACTIONS THAT COULD BE SUBJECT TO NOLLAN/DOLAN SCRUTINY, YES, JUSTICE THOMAS."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. McGRATH",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "UNDER CALIFORNIA LAW, IT IS NOT A TAX, BUT I THINK, FOR PURPOSES OF CONSTITUTIONAL LAW, IT IS A TAX."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. McGRATH",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do think the Due Process Clause would provide a check there. And I also think that the Court could reason by analogy to the special assessment and the user fee cases, where the Court has made clear that despite the deference that legislatures receive in this area, they have to act reasonably."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: What's the difference between reasonableness as you're describing it and rough proportionality and essential -- and nexus?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: When you talk about due process, are you talking about substantive or procedural due process?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ross",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0004-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I think this goes to the point that no court or this Court at least to my knowledge has never held that a widely applicable fee paid by large numbers of people to pay for government infrastructure is a taking, and I think doing so in this case would be -- would be very disruptive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, you -- you said that there would be no takings analysis with respect to a widely applicable provision that covers a large number of people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Yeah, but, I mean, obviously, that's a broad range. And I'm just trying to get a sense of exactly where you would have -- I mean, because this is a threshold determination, but if it depends on individualized analysis and you've got to figure out, well, where along that spectrum does it apply, that's not a very helpful threshold."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b637fba0d78d34f2b7a82c16a4e8a4de0eafbc8acaa217f745efb853c25c5fe5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b637fba0d78d-0004-0011",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 100,
        "start": 100
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1074",
